farcli recording 1
app: claude
app-version: 2.1.322 (Claude Code)
system: Windows native
size: 100x30
cursor: 0,0
command: claude --safe-mode --model haiku --resume 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
windows-version: Microsoft Windows [Version 10.0.22631.6199]
hidden-terminal: Microsoft.Windows.Console.ConPTY 1.25.261109001, shipped with farcli
display-mode: fullscreen (CLAUDE_CODE_NO_FLICKER=1)
holds: not a model's reply: a copy of an earlier session's transcript in which the reply was replaced by hand with the Markdown text in claude-fullscreen-markdown-shapes.reply.md, started again with --resume so that Claude Code draws it. It shows how Claude Code draws lines separated by single line breaks, code blocks with and without a language, a heading, a quotation, a link, inline code, and list items that wrap; then the mouse wheel turned up and down forty times each, and Page Up and Page Down five times each; nothing is typed or sent
arguments: --safe-mode keeps the user's own settings, plugins and servers out; --model haiku keeps the reply cheap; DISABLE_NON_ESSENTIAL_MODEL_CALLS=1 was set as well
environment: as PowerShell in Windows Terminal has it: only the variables Windows keeps for the machine and the user, plus WT_SESSION and WT_PROFILE_ID; no NO_COLOR, TERM, COLORTERM or TERM_PROGRAM
terminal: the stand-in Terminal says where its cursor is and what kind of terminal it is, and gives Windows Terminal's default colours (text cccccc, background 0c0c0c) when asked for them
made-with: examples/hidden_terminal_probe played claude-fullscreen-markdown-shapes.steps into farcli on a hidden terminal, with nobody at the keyboard

